hadiths[106]{hadithnumber,text}:
"4297","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub did not tell us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, he said: He told me Hussein bin Abdullah bin Ubaid Allah bin Abbas, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both. Ibn Ishaq said: He told me Yazid bin Ruman, on the authority of Urwa bin Al-Zubayr, who said: “Atika bint Abdul Muttalib, may God be pleased with her, saw what the sleeper sees before the onset of Damam ibn Amr al-Ghaffari visited the Quraysh in Mecca three nights after a vision, and in the morning A’tika venerated her, so she sent for her brother. Al-Abbas bin Abdul Muttalib, and she said to him: O brother, tonight I saw a vision that frightened me, lest some evil come upon your people. And an affliction. He said: What is it? She said: I saw, as the sleeper saw, that a man came to his camel and stopped with the pad, and said: Depart, O people of treachery, for your battles in three days. So I saw the people gathered to him, then I saw his camel entering the mosque with it, and the people gathered to it, then his camel appeared with it, and behold, it was on its head. The Kaaba, so he said: Depart, O people of treachery, to fight yours in three days. Then his camel was mounted on the head of Abu Qubays, so he said: Depart, O people of treachery. To wrestle with you in three days. Then he took a rock and sent it down from the top of the mountain.So it began to fall until it was at the bottom of the mountain, and it declined, and not a house remained of your people, nor a house, but some of them entered it. Al-Abbas said: By God, this is a vision, so conceal it. She said: And you, conceal it. If this reaches Quraysh, they will harm us. So he left. Al-Abbas then met Al-Walid bin Utba, who was a friend of his, so he mentioned it to him and he kept it secret, so Al-Walid mentioned it to his father. So he spoke about it, and the conversation became widespread. Al-Abbas said: By God, I was going to go to the Kaaba to circumambulate it when I entered the mosque, and behold, Abu Ignorance about a group of Quraysh talking about a vision of Atika, so Abu Jahl said: O Abu Al-Fadl, when did this prophetess speak to you? I said: What is that? He said: A vision that Atika bint Abdul Muttalib saw. Are you not satisfied, O Banu Abdul Muttalib, for your men to prophesy? Until your women prophesy, we will wait for you. These three things that Atika mentioned. If it is true, it will be so. Otherwise, We will write a decree against you. You are the most liarous family in the Arabs. By God, he did not think of anything significant from me except that I denied what she said, so I said: She did not see anything nor I heard about this, and in the evening there was not a woman left from the Banu Abdul Muttalib who did not come to me and say: Have you been patient with this evil, evil debauchee? It falls on your feet,Then he dealt with women while you were listening, and you had no jealousy about that? So I said: By God, you have told me the truth, and I had no qualms about that except that I denied what he said, so if he came back, I would protect him, so I sat in On the third day, I went up to him so he could say something, and I insulted him. By God, I was heading towards him. He was a man with a sharp face and a sharp appearance. The iron of the tongue became sharp as it turned towards the door of the mosque, so I said to myself: O God, curse all of this rather than insulting him, and behold, he He heard what I did not hear, the voice of Damdam bin Amr as he was standing on his camel in Al-Abtah. He had turned his mount, torn his shirt, and trodden his camel. He says: O people of Quraysh, the kind and the kind are your wealth with Abu Sufyan, and your trade was offered to Muhammad and his companions, so relief, That distracted him from me, so there was nothing but the defense until we left, and he attacked Quraysh as he had struck on the day of Badr, by killing their nobles, and he was taken prisoner. Their choice. Atika bint Abdul Muttalib said:
 [Long Sea]

 Wasn't the vision true and he criticized you for believing it? Few of the people escaped.
 So you said, ""I did not lie. I lied. Rather... they deny the truth about someone who is a liar.""
 He told a long story
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4297 - Hussein is weak"
"4298","Ishaq bin Abdullah bin Ishaq Al-Baghawi told us, Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi told us, Abu Thabit told us, Ibn Wahb told me, Abu Sakhr told me, on the authority of Abu Muawiyah al-Bajli, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that Ali ibn Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him, He said to him: “We had nothing with us except two knights, a horse belonging to Al-Zubayr, and a horse belonging to Al-Miqdad ibn Al-Aswad - meaning the day of Badr -” This is an authentic hadith subject to the conditions. The two Sheikhs, “Abu Thabit is Muhammad bin Ubayd Allah Al-Madani, Abu Sakhr is Humaid bin Ziyad, and Abu Muawiyah Al-Bajli Ammar Al-Dahni, and they all agreed upon it, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4298 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4299","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Abu Al-Muthanna Muadh bin Al-Muthanna told us, Abu Al-Walid Al-Tayalisi told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zirr, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: On the day of Badr, we were all three riding a camel. He said: Ali and Abu Lubabah were companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: And when it was his obstacle, we would say: Ride until we walk, and he would say: “You are not stronger than me, and I am not richer in reward.” “From among you.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it."
"4300","Abu Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Yahya and Abu Al-Hussein bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz narrated to us, saying: Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Thaqafi narrated to us, narrated to us Qutayba bin Saeed, Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Abdullah, may God be pleased with him, on the Night of Decree, he said: “They searched for it for eleven days, on the morning of the day of Badr.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4300 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4301","Abu Ishaq and Abu Al-Hussein told us, they said: Muhammad bin Qutaibah told us, Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Abd God, may God be pleased with him, said: “Seek Laylat al-Qadr on the nineteenth of the morning of the day of Badr, the day of separation, the day the two hosts meet.” This “A hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4301 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4302","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Ali bin Al-Hassan bin Abi Issa told us, Abdul-Malik bin Ibrahim Al-Jdi told us, Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Ishaq Al-Hamdani, who said: I heard Al-Bara’ bin Aazib saying: “The emigrants on the day of Badr were eighty-odd or so, and there were “The Ansar, two hundred and forty-odd.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4302 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4303","Abu Al-Walid Al-Faqih told me, Al-Hasan bin Sufyan told us, Abu Bakr bin Abi Shaybah told us, Abu Nu’aym told us, Abd Al-Rahman bin Al-Ghasil told us, On the authority of Hamza bin Abi Usayd, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said on the day of Badr when we lined up to fight to the Quraysh and they lined up for us: “If they attack you, shoot them with arrows.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4303 - True"
"4304","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Jarir told us, about Al-A'mash, on the authority of Amr ibn Murrah, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah ibn Abdullah, on the authority of his father, who said: When it was the day of Badr, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to them Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “What do you say about these captives?” Then Abdullah bin Rawaha said: Come to a valley abounding with firewood, light a fire, then throw them in. In it, Al-Abbas, may God be pleased with him, said: May God cut off your ties of kinship, and Omar, may God be pleased with him, said: Their leaders and chiefs killed you and denied you. Then strike their necks again. Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him, said: Your clan and your people. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered to meet some of them. His need, so a group said: What Omar said, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came out and said: “What do you say about these people?” Indeed, the likeness of these is like that of their brothers who were before them. {Noah said, “My Lord, do not leave on earth an abode of the disbelievers.” [Noah: 26] And He said Moses: {Our Lord, destroy their wealth and strengthen their hearts} [Yunus: 88] the verse, and Abraham said: {So whoever follows me is of me, and whoever disobeys me. For indeed, You are Forgiving and Merciful} [Ibrahim: 36] And Jesus said: {If You punish them, then they are Your servants, and if You forgive them, then indeed You are the Mighty, the Wise} [Al-Maeda: 118] And you are a people who are fierce among you, so none of you will surrender except by ransom or by beheading.” Abdullah said: So I said: Except Suhail bin White, for he cannot be killed. I heard him speaking about Islam, but I remained silent. There was never a day when I was afraid that stones from the sky would be thrown at me. From that day until the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Except Suhail bin Bayda.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4304 - True"
"4305","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, he said: Abdul told me Allah bin Abi Bakr, on the authority of Yahya bin Abdullah bin Abdul Rahman bin Asaad bin Zurarah, on the authority of his grandfather, who said: He brought the captives when He brought them to Medina, and Sawda bint Zamaa, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was with the Afra’ family in their mourning over Awf and Mu’awwidha, the sons of Afra. - And that was before the veil was drawn over them - Sawda said: By God, I was with them when we came, and it was said: These prisoners have come. With them, I returned to my house, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was in it, and I saw Abu Yazid Suhail bin Amr in the direction of the room, and his hands Two groups tied a rope around his neck. By God, when I saw Abu Yazid, I had no power to say: Abu Yazid, did you give with your own hands unless he died? Honorable? I only noticed what the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said from the house: “O Sawdah, upon God and upon His Messenger,” so I said: O Messenger of God, By the One who sent you with the truth, when I saw Abu Yazid placing his hands with a rope around his neck, I had no power to say what I said: “This is an authentic hadith on the authority of The condition of a Muslim, and they did not narrate it.” The two sheikhs agreed to narrate the hadith of Muhammad bin Fulayh, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, who said: Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, narrated to us that some Ansar asked permission from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and they said: O Messenger of God, Give us permission to leave the ransom to our sister’s son, Abbas, and he said: “By God, do not leave a dirham.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4305 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"4306","Abu Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, he said: He told me Yahya bin Abbad bin Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: When the people of Mecca were sent to sacrifice They captured them. Zainab, the daughter of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was sent to ransom Abu Al-Aas with money that contained a necklace that Khadija had brought to her. Abi Al-Aas when he built on it, and when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw it, he was very kind to it and said: “If you decide to release it her captive and return to her what is hers.” The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, had taken charge of him, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, promised that Zainab tells him, “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and he did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4306 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"4307","Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Salamah Al-Anazi told me, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told me, Abdullah bin Salih told us, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Salih, on the authority of Ali Ibn Abi Talha, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, in His Almighty and Majestic saying: {If you believe in God and in what We have revealed to Our servant The Day of Criterion} [Al-Anfal: 41] “What is meant by the Criterion is: the Day of Badr, the day God separated between truth and falsehood.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration. He brings him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4307 - True"
"4308","Abu Al-Hussein bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told me, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Thaqafi told me, Abu Hashim Ziyad bin Ayyub told us, Marwan bin Muawiyah told us. Al-Fazari, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ayman al-Makki told us, on the authority of Ubaid ibn Rafi’ al-Zarqi, on the authority of his father, who said: When it was the day of Uhud, the polytheists retreated, The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Stay straight until I praise my Lord, the Mighty and Majestic.” So they formed ranks behind him, and he said: “O God, all praise is due to You. O God, there is no one to seize what You have extended, no one to extend what You have taken, no guide to whom You have led astray, no misguided to whom You have guided, no giver what You have withheld, and no hinderer. for what You have given, and there is no one who can bring it closer when you are far away, and there is no one who can distance one from what you have brought near. O God, extend upon us your blessings, mercy, grace, and provision. O God, I I ask you for eternal bliss that does not change or fade away. Oh God, I ask you for security on the day of fear. Oh God, I seek refuge from the evil of what you have given us and the evil of what You prevented us, O God, make faith beloved to us and beautify it in our hearts, and make disbelief, immorality, and disobedience hateful to us, and make us among the rightly guided ones. We died as Muslims, and we lived as Muslims, and join us with the righteous, without disgrace or being tempted. O God, kill the infidels who deny Your messengers. And they turn away from Your path, and inflict upon them Your punishment and Your torment. O God of truth, Amen.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4308 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4309","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Abu Al-Hasan Ali bin Muhammad Al-Thaqafi told us in Kufa, Munjab bin Al-Harith Al-Tamimi told us. He said: Sufyan bin Uyaynah claimed, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: Ali, may God be pleased with them, came On the day of Uhud, he bent down with his sword and said to Fatima, may God be pleased with her: “Hold the sword, praiseworthy, for she has healed me.” The Messenger of God, may God bless her, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “If you are good at striking with your sword, Sahl bin Hanif, Abu Dujana, and Asim bin Thabit Al-Aflah have been good at it. And Al-Harith bin Al-Simah said: “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, and they did not narrate it.” And he has authentic witness in the battles.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4309 - According to Al-Bukhari’s condition"
"4310","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, he said: Hussein told me Bin Abdullah bin Ubaid Allah bin Abbas, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, returned When he greeted, he gave his sword to his daughter Fatima, and said: “Daughter, wash away this blood.” Then Ali gave her his sword, and said: “And wash away this blood.” His blood. By God, the fighting has been true to me today. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If you believed the fighting today, he has been true to you.” The fighting today is Sahl bin Hunaif and Samak bin Kharsha Abu Dujana.” Ibn Ishaq said: Ali bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him, said When he handed the sword to Fatima, peace be upon her.
 [Long Sea]
 I am not reprehensible to the one who wields the sword... I am neither arrogant nor mean.
 By my life, I have been excused in Nasr Ahmad...and the pleasures of a Lord who is merciful to His servants.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4310 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4311","Abu Al-Hussein Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Tamim Al-Qantari told me, in Baghdad, Abu Ismail Al-Sulami told us, Sulayman bin Ayyub bin Suleiman bin Musa bin Talha Al-Talhi, my father told me, on the authority of my grandfather, on the authority of Musa bin Talha, on the authority of his father, Talha bin Ubaidullah, may God be pleased with him. He said: When it was the day of Uhud, she shook with this poetry:
 [The sea of rage]

 We are the protectors of a conqueror and a master... We defend on behalf of our blessed Messenger.
 We fight against him today in battles... he struck the battlefield in Al-Mubarak.
 . When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, departed on the day of Uhud, he said to Hassan: “Say about Talha,” so Hassan rose up and said:
 [Long Sea]

 Talha on the Day of Shaab made Muhammad sad... on a path that was difficult and difficult for him.
 He protected him with his palms and spears, and I surrendered... I encouraged him under swords, but they were paralyzed.
 And he was the imam of the people except Muhammad... He established the millstone of Islam until it stood firm.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4311 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4312","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, he said: So he told me Yahya bin Abbad bin Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather Al-Zubayr, may God be pleased with him, who said: “So I saw the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He greeted him when he went to get up to the rock, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, appeared between two shields, but he was unable to get up. To it, so Talha bin Ubaid Allah sat under it, then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, got up until he sat on top of it, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: He said: “Talha made it obligatory.” This is an authentic hadith according to Muslim’s condition, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4312 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"4313","Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told me, Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, Al-Hasan bin Issa told us, Ibn Al-Mubarak told us, Ishaq bin Yahya informed us, Musa bin Talha told me, “Talha returned with thirty-seven or thirty-five wounds, a wound, a stab wound, and a shot. His forehead was covered with pearls. “His index finger was cut off, and the next finger was paralyzed.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4313 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4314","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Ishaq, on the authority of Uthman bin Abdul Al-Rahman, on the authority of Aisha bint Saad, on the authority of her father Saad bin Abi Waqqas, may God be pleased with him, who said: When people went around the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him He delivered that tour on Uhud. I stepped aside and said: I will defend myself. Either I will be martyred, or I will escape until I meet the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. While I was like that, a man with a veil of veil appeared on his face. I do not know who he was. The polytheists approached until I said: They have mounted him. his hand of pebbles, then he threw it in their faces, and they fell backwards on their heels until they came to the mountain. He did that repeatedly, and I do not know who he was. And between me and him was Al-Miqdad ibn Al-Aswad, and between us I wanted to ask Al-Miqdad about him, when Al-Miqdad said: O Sa’d, this is the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, is calling you. I said: Where is he? Al-Miqdad pointed to him, so I stood up, as if no harm had befallen me. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Where have you been today?” Oh Saad? So I said: Where I saw the Messenger of God and he made me sit in front of him, so I started shooting and saying: Oh God, throw your arrow with it at your enemy and at the Messenger of God, may God bless him. And he said: “O God, respond to Sa’d. Oh God, repay Sa’d for what you shot. O Sa’d, may my father and mother be sacrificed for you.” There is no arrow I shoot without, and he said The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “O God, direct his shot, and answer his supplication, O Sa’d.” Even when I finished my quiver, the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said He, peace and blessings be upon him, handed over what was in his quiver, so he presented me with a fresh arrow. He said: It is the one with feathers, and it was stronger than others. Al-Zuhri said: “Indeed, the arrows that “Saad shot a thousand arrows at it that day.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4314 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"4315","Abu Bakr bin Abi Dharm, Al-Hafiz, in Kufa, told us, Muhammad bin Uthman bin Abi Shaybah told us, Manjab bin Al-Harith told us, Ali bin Abu Bakr Al-Razi, Muhammad bin Ishaq bin Yahya bin Talha told us, on the authority of Musa bin Talha, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: He said Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq, may God be pleased with him: “When people came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the day of Uhud: I was the first to come to the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. I looked at him from a distance, and behold, I saw a man who embraced me from behind me like a bird, seeking the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. So, behold, it is Abu Ubaidah bin Al-Jarrah, and behold, there is a man who raises it one time and puts it down again, so I said: What if he made me mistaken because I was I am with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Talha comes and that is the one I and I command, so we end up with him, then Talha raises him once and puts him down. Another, and behold, he was shot with sixty-six wounds, one of which cut off his ankle. Then, behold, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was struck on the His cheeks, and two rings from the Forgiver’s ring were stuck to his cheeks. When Abu Ubaidah saw what was wrong with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he pleaded with me to God for what If you were alone between me and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he grabbed one of them with his fold and extended it and it receded and his fold receded, then he looked To the other, and God called me to me when I was alone with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so he took hold of it with the other fold, and extended it, and it receded. Its folds became rare, so Abu Ubaidah made the folds thin. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4315 - Ibn Ishaq is abandoned"
"4316","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, he said: So he told me Yahya bin Abbad bin Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, that Al-Zubayr bin Al-Awwam, may God be pleased with him, said: “By God, You saw me looking at Hind bint Utbah and her companions, uncovered, fleeing, without taking them either little or much, as the archers tended to The army, until we discovered the people who wanted to plunder, and they left our backs to the horses, so we turned back, and a loud man shouted, except that Muhammad He was killed, so we withdrew, and the people withdrew after we hit the banner until none of the people approached it. This is an authentic hadith subject to the condition. Muslim and they did not produce it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4316 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"4317","Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, “that Amr bin Qais had a lord in the pre-Islamic period, and he was That Lord prevented him from Islam until he took it, so one day the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and his companions came to Uhud and said: Where is Saad? Ibn Muadh? It was said about Uhud, and he said: Where are his brother’s sons? It was said: By Uhud, so he asked about his people. They said: By Uhud. So he took his sword and spear, and put on his headdress, then he went to Uhud, and when he saw him Muslims, they said: Here on our behalf, O Amr. He said: I have believed, so he was carried and fought, so he was carried to his family wounded, then Saad bin Muadh entered upon him, and he said To him: Did you come to anger God and His Messenger or to protect your people? He said: “Rather, I came in the wrath of God and His Messenger.” Abu Hurairah said: “Then he entered Paradise and did not pray a single prayer for God,” according to the condition of a Muslim.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4317 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"4318","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, he said: Asim told me Ibn Omar Ibn Qatada, on the authority of Abdul Rahman Ibn Jabir Ibn Abdullah, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with him, who said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And when he mentions the companions of Uhud, he says: “By God, I wish I were betrayed with my companions in the embrace of the mountain.” He says: “I was killed with them.”"
"4319","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Abu Bakr bin Abi Al-Dunya Al-Qurashi told us, Ali bin Shuaib told me, Ibn Abu Fudayk, Suleiman bin Dawud told me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ja’far bin Muhammad, on the authority of his father, that his father, Ali bin Al-Hussein, told him about His father, “Fatima, the daughter of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to visit the grave of her uncle Hamza bin Abdul Muttalib during the days, and she would pray and cry.” “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4319 - Suleiman bin Daoud Madani spoke about it"
"4320","Abu Bakr Ismail bin Muhammad bin Ismail al-Faqih told us about Rayy, Muhammad bin al-Mughirah al-Sukari told us, Abd al-Rahman bin Alqama told us. Al-Marwazi, Al-Attaf bin Khalid Al-Makhzoumi told us, Abdul-Ala bin Abdullah bin Abi Farwa told me, on the authority of his father, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, visited the graves of the martyrs in Uhud and said: “O God, your servant and your Prophet bear witness that these are martyrs, and that he who visited them And he greeted them until the Day of Resurrection. They responded to him.” Al-Attaf said: My aunt told me that she visited the graves of the martyrs. She said: “And there is no one with me except Two boys were watching over the animal. She said: So I greeted them and heard a return of greetings. They said: By God, we know you as we know each other. She said: Then I shivered, so I said: O boy, bring my mule, so I mounted. “This is an authentic Madani chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4320 - Sent"
"4321","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Abu Al-Nadr told us, Abu Sa’id Al-Muaddeb told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, On the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, that she said to Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr, may God be pleased with them both: “O son of my sister, by God Indeed, your father and your grandfather means Abu Bakr and Al-Zubayr, may God be pleased with them, among those. God Almighty said: {Those who responded to God and the Messenger from After the ulcer struck them.} [Al Imran: 172] “This is an authentic hadith, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4321 - True"
"4322","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us, Muhammad bin Muadh told us, Abu Al-Nu’man Muhammad bin Al-Fadl Arim told us, Abu Awanah told us, On the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Sulayman bin Qais, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, fought a warrior A stand of a palm tree, and they saw that the Muslims were surprised, then a man from among them called Ghawarth bin Al-Harith came until he stood on the head of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted him with the sword, and said: Who will prevent you from me? He said: “God.” He said: Then the sword fell from his hand, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took it and said: “Who will stop you?” He said: Be the best taker. He said: “Do you bear witness that there is no god but God and that I am the Messenger of God?” He said: I promise you that I will not fight you, nor will I be with a people who fight you. He said: So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, left his way and came to His people, and he said: I came to you from the best of people. When the time for prayer came, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, performed the prayer of fear, and the people were in two groups. A group was facing the enemy, and a group was praying with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. So he led those with him in prayer two rak’ahs, so they departed and were in a place. Those who were fighting against their enemy, and those came and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, led two rak’ahs with them, and it was two rak’ahs for the people. Two rak’ahs, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, has four rak’ahs. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4322 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4323","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Al-Nadr Abi Umar, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them, said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, went out on a campaign and met the polytheists at Usfan. When the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, prayed, At noon, may God bless him and grant him peace, they saw him bowing and prostrating, he and his companions. Then some of them said to one another: This was an opportunity for you if you were tempted. They will not know about you until you agree with them. Then one of them said: They have another prayer, which is more beloved to them than their families and their wealth. So prepare until you attack them therein, so God Almighty and Majestic revealed to His Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: {And when you are among them, you establish the prayer for them} [An-Nisa: 102] Until the end of the verse, and He taught him what the polytheists were commanded to do, “When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed the afternoon prayer, and they were facing him in He placed the Muslims in two rows behind him, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said “Allahu Akbar,” so “Allahu Akbar” with him. He mentioned the prayer of fear, and said at the end of it: When the polytheists looked at him, some prostrated and some stood looking at them, and they said: They have been informed of what we wanted. This is an authentic hadith. According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4323 - According to Al-Bukhari’s condition"
"4324","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Abu Asim told us, and Abu Amr bin Abi Ja’far Al-Muqri told us And the word for it is: Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman told us, Amr bin Ali told us, Abu Asim told us, Hanzalah bin Abi Sufyan told us, Saeed bin Abi Sufyan told us. Mina said: I heard Jabir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with them both, saying: When the trench was dug, I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, severe oppression. He said: So I turned to my wife and said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, suffering severe hardship, so she brought out to me a bag containing a saa’ of Barley, and we have a domesticated animal. He said: I slaughtered it and ground it a saa’, so I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I consulted with him and said: O Messenger of God, We have slaughtered an animal for ourselves, and I have ground a sa` of barley that we had, so come, you and a group with you. He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, shouted: “Oh! People of the Trench, Jabir has built a wall and greets you. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do not put down your whole cloak and do not bake it.” I made your dough until I come.” He said: So I came and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came, and the people came forward until my wife came and she brought out dough for him. So he spat in it and blessed it, then he said: “Call for me a baker, and she will bake with you. Empty your wheat, and do not put it down.” And they were a thousand, so he swore He will be rewarded by God Almighty. They ate until they left and went away, and indeed our wheat would be covered as it is, and our dough would be baked as it is. This is the wording. The hadith of Abu Amr in the wording of Abu Abbas is a summary. This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4324 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4325","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Kamil Al-Qadi told us, Issa bin Abdullah Al-Tayalisi told us, Abu Nu’aym Al-Fadl bin Dukayn told us, Yusuf bin Abd told us. Allah bin Abi Burdah, on the authority of Musa bin Al-Mukhtar, on the authority of Bilal Al-Absi, on the authority of Hudhayfah bin Al-Yaman, may God be pleased with them both, that the people dispersed from The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the night of the battles, and only twelve men remained with him. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to me while I He knelt down from the cold, and said: “O son of Yaman, get up and go to the army of the parties and look at their condition.” I said: O Messenger of God, and who He sent you with the truth. I did not come to you except out of shame because of the cold. He said: “Go out of the heat and the cold of the morning. Go, O son of Yaman, and there is no problem. Heat and cold are upon you until you return to me.” He said: So I went to their camp and found Abu Sufyan lighting a fire in a group around him that had dispersed. Al-Ahzab on his authority. He said: Until I sat among them. He said: Abu Sufyan thought that someone else had entered among them. He said: Let every man be taken. of you in the hand of his companion. He said: So I struck my hand on the one on my right and took his hand. Then I struck my hand on the one on my left and I took his hand. So I stayed with them for a while, then I got up and went to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was standing and praying, and he motioned to me with his hand to approach, so I approached. Then he also motioned for me to come closer, so I approached until some of the garment that was on him while he was praying dripping on me. When he finished his prayer, he said: “Ibn Al-Yaman, sit down. What’s the matter? I said: O Messenger of God, the people dispersed from Abu Sufyan, and all that remained was a group that kindled the fire. God had poured upon him as much hail as he had poured. upon us, but we hope from God what he does not hope for. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4325 - True"
"4326","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Miqsam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: A man from the polytheists was killed on the day of the ditch, so they asked to hide him. “Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, refused until they gave him the blood money.” Among the Banu Amir bin Luay, Amr bin Abd Wadd was killed, and Ali bin Abi Talib Mubarakah: “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.” “And it has an amazing witness.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4326 - True"
"4327","Lu’u’ bin Abdullah Al-Muqaddri told us, in the Caliph’s palace in Baghdad, Abu Al-Tayyib Ahmad bin Ibrahim bin Abdul-Wahhab told us. Al-Masry, in Damascus, Ahmed bin Issa Al-Khashab told us, in Tennis, Amr bin Abi Salamah told us, Sufyan Al-Thawri told us, on the authority of Bahz bin Hakim, on the authority of His father, on the authority of his grandfather, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “To Ali bin Abi Talib’s duel with Amr bin Abd Wad on the day of the Trench.” Better than the deeds of my nation until the Day of Resurrection.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4327 - May God disgrace a Rafidite who slanders him"
"4328","So Ismail bin Muhammad bin Al-Fadl Al-Sha’arani told us, Jeddi told us, Ibrahim bin Al-Mundhir Al-Hazami told us, Muhammad bin Falih told us, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, said: “Among the polytheists was killed on the day of the Trench. Amr ibn Abd Wad was killed by Ali ibn Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him.” On his authority, “The chain of transmission of this battle is authentic according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs.”"
"4329","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, he said: Amr bin Abd Wad was the third leader of Quraysh. He had fought on the Day of Badr until he was healed by surgery, and he did not witness anyone. So when it was the day of the Trench, he went out. A teacher to see his scene, and when he and his horses stopped, Ali said to him: O Amr, you were promising God to the Quraysh that he would not invite a man to two meetings. Unless you accept one of them from him, then Amr said: Yes, then Ali, may God be pleased with him, said to him: I invite you to God Almighty and to His Messenger. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him and Islam. He said: I have no need for that. He said: I am inviting you to defecate. He said: My nephew, why? By God, I do not like to kill you, so Ali said: But I would like to kill you, so Amr became hot, so he jumped from his horse and maimed it, then he came back. So he came to Ali and said: Who will duel? Then Ali stood up while he was masked in iron and said: I am his, O Prophet of God. He said: It is Amr bin Abd Wad, sit down. Amr called out: Don’t you? A man? “So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave him permission.” Then Ali, may God be pleased with him, walked to him and said:
 [full sea]

 Do not be hasty, for he has come to you... He will answer your voice, not powerless.
 He has intelligence and insight...and honesty is the savior of every winner.I hope to perform a funeral mourning over you...
 From the blow of Najla... whose remembrance remains with those who shake it.
 Amr said to him: Who are you? He said: I am Ali. He said: Whose son? He said: Ibn Abd Manaf, I am Ali bin Abi Talib. He said: You have, O my nephew, one of your paternal uncles who is older than you, so leave. I will go away. I hate to shed your blood. Ali said: But by God, I do not hate to shed your blood. So he got angry, so he came down and unsheathed his sword as if it were a flame of fire. Then he came towards Ali angrily, and Ali greeted him with his shield, and Amr hit him in the shield, causing him to lose it, and he stuck the sword in it and hit his head. So he attacked him, and Ali, may God be pleased with him, hit him on the rope, so he fell and revolted, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, heard the takbeer being said, so he knew That Ali killed him, then Ali, may God Almighty be pleased with him, says:

 Why should the knights attack me like this... On my behalf and on their behalf, they delayed my companions?
 Today, my anger prevents me from escaping... and there is a designer in my head that is not my style.
 Except for Ibn Abd when he insisted on it... And I swore, “Listen from the Book.”
 I do not believe those who praise piety... two men who strike every striker.
 So when I left him, it became tangled... like a log between your steps and my hills.
 And I pardoned his clothes, even though... I was the distiller weighing my clothes.He worshiped stones out of the foolishness of his mind... and I worshiped the Lord of Muhammad rightly
 Then Ali, may God be pleased with him, approached the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and his face was beaming, and Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, said: Could you please rob him of his armor? The Arabs have no armor better than this. So he said: I struck him and he defeated me with his armor, and I was ashamed for my cousin to rob him. His horses came out defeated, until they were pushed out of the ditch."
"4330","Abu Bakr bin Darim Al-Hafiz told us, Al-Mundhir bin Muhammad Al-Lakhmi told us, Ubayy told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Abbad bin Hani told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq bin Yassar said: Asim bin Omar bin Qatada told me: “When Ali bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him, killed Amr bin Abd Wad had his sister Amra bint Abd Wad mourn him and said:
 [Simple Sea]
 If the killer of Amr had been other than his killer... I would have cried for him as long as the soul had not stayed in my body.
 But he was killed by someone who did not blame him...and in the past he was called Bayd al-Balad. “And I heard Abu Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub, I heard Ahmad bin Abd The mighty Mercury, I heard Yahya bin Adam saying: “I did not liken the killing of Ali to Omar except with the words of God Almighty: {So they defeated them, by permission. God and David killed Goliath} """"
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4330 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4330 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4331","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Baghdadi told us, Abu Ulatha Muhammad bin Khalid told us, Ubi told us, Ibn Lahi’ah told us, he said: Urwa bin Al-Zubayr said: “Among the infidels of Quraysh was killed on the Day of the Trench, from Banu Amir bin Luay, then from Banu Malik bin Hasal, Amr bin Abd Wad bin Nasr bin Malik bin Hasal was killed by Ali bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him. “I mentioned about the killing of Amr bin Abd A number of supported hadiths and together, on the authority of Urwa ibn al-Zubayr, Musa ibn Uqba, and Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Yasar, what has reached me to be confirmed According to Al-Munsif among the scholars, Amr ibn Abd Wad did not kill him, and no one participated in his killing except the Commander of the Faithful, Ali ibn Ubayy. Talib, may God be pleased with him. What prompted me to investigate this matter was the statement of one of the Kharijites who said: “Muhammad ibn Maslamah also He struck him and took some of the loot. By God, we have not heard of this from any of the Companions and Followers, may God be pleased with them. How is it possible? And Ali, may God be pleased with him, said: “We have not heard that I refrained from robbing my cousin, so I left him.” This is his answer to the Commander of the Faithful, Omar. Ibn Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, in the presence of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.”"
"4332","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Kamil Al-Qadi told us, Muhammad bin Musa bin Hammad Al-Barbari told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Abu Abdullah Al-Musaybi told us, Abdullah bin Nafi’ told us, Abdullah bin Omar told us, on the authority of his brother Ubayd Allah bin Omar, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Muhammad, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her The wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was with her, and a man from the household greeted us while we were in the house. Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, got up in fright, so I got up after him, and behold, Dihya al-Kalbi, and he said: “This is Gabriel commanding me to go.” To Banu Qurayza,” and he said: “You have laid down your weapons, but we did not give up. We pursued the polytheists until we reached the Red Lion,” and that was when he returned. The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came out of the trench, and the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, got up in fear and said to his companions: “I have determined that you will not pray a prayer. afternoon until you came to Banu Qurayzah.” Then the sun set before they came to them, and a group of Muslims said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not He wanted them to call off the prayer, so they prayed, and a group said: We are following the resolve of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and there is no sin upon us, so a group prayed out of faith. And out of hope, and a group left out of faith and out of hope, and the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, did not criticize any of the two groups, and the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, went out and passed. During a session between him and Qurayza, he said: “Did anyone pass by you?” They said: Dihya al-Kalbi passed by us on a gray mule with a brocade velor underneath. He said: “That is not Dihya al-Kalbi, but it is Gabriel sent.” To Banu Qurayzah to shake them and cast terror into their hearts.” So the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, besieged them and ordered his companions to take cover. So he besieged them, so he besieged them. Until they came down on the rule of Saad bin Muadh, and they were his allies, so it was decided that those who fight against them should be killed, and their descendants and women taken captive. “This An authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs. For they used Abdullah bin Omar Al-Amri as evidence in the evidence, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4332 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4333","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Abu Muslim told us, Hajjaj bin Minhal told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Umair. He said: Attiya al-Qurazi told me, he said: “We were presented to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, at the time of Qurayzah. He was killed, so they looked at me, but my pubic hair had not grown, so I was left” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not take it out. It has a chain of narrations, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Umair, including al-Thawri, Shu`bah, and Zuhayr.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4333 - True"
"4334","Abu Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, he said: Muhammad told me Ibn Ja`far Ibn al-Zubayr, on the authority of Urwa Ibn al-Zubayr, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, that she said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was not killed.” Not a single woman from Banu Qurayza greeted anyone except one woman. By God, she makes me laugh from the back of my stomach, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And he went to kill their men with swords, when he called out her name: Where is so-and-so? She said: I swear by God. I said: Woe to you, what is the matter with you? She said: I will be killed, by God. I said: Why? She said: Because of an incident that happened to him. So he set off with her and beheaded her. I will never forget how amazingly good she was. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4334 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4335","Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Salamah Al-Anazi told me, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Abu Al-Walid told us, Ikrimah bin Ammar told us, and Muhammad told us Bin Ibrahim bin Al-Fadl Al-Hashimi, and the pronunciation for him, Ahmed bin Salamah told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Abu Amir told us, Ikrimah told us Ibn Ammar, on the authority of Iyas Ibn Salamah, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with them, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave orders over us to Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with them. On his authority, we attacked people from Bani Fazara, and when we approached a vessel, Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him, ordered us to celebrate the wedding. When we prayed the morning prayer, Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him, ordered us to launch the raid. He said: We brought water and with it we killed whoever killed us. He said: Then a group of people left. Among them were the children and the women. They had almost raced to the mountain, so We put an arrow between them and the mountain. When they saw the arrow, they stopped, and I came. I will take them to Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him, and among them is a woman from Banu Fazara who has a dimple of blood on her, and with her is a daughter of hers. He is the best of the Arabs. He said: Then Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him, sent her daughter to me. He said: I came to Medina, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, met me. In the market, he said: “O Salamah, by God, your father has given me the woman.” So I said: By God, O Messenger of God, I have not uncovered a garment for her, and she is yours, O Messenger of God. Messenger of God, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent it to Mecca, and ransomed with it Muslim prisoners who were in the hands of the polytheists. It was narrated by a Muslim without this context.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4335 - Narrated by Muslim with another interpretation"
"4336","Abu Amr Uthman bin Ahmad bin Al-Sammak told us, in Baghdad, Abdul-Rahman bin Muhammad Al-Harithi told us, Yahya bin Saeed Al-Qattan told us, Muhammad bin Abi Yahya Al-Aslami told us, my father told me that Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, told him that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him He was in Al-Hudaybiyyah and said: “Do not light a fire at night.” When it was after that, he said: “Light it and create it, for no people will know “After you, your saa’ or your mudd” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4336 - True"
"4337","Khuthaym bin Arak, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: “When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out to Khaybar, he appointed Siba’ bin Arafat Al-Ghafari in Medina” is authentic
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4337 - True"
"4338","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, he said: Tell me Buraidah bin Sufyan bin Buraidah Al-Aslami, on the authority of Salama bin Amr bin Al-Akwa’, may God be pleased with him, said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was sent Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him, surrendered to some of the forts of Khaybar, and he fought and struggled, but there was no conquest. This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and it was not They bring it out. “Abu Qutaybah Salim bin Al-Fasl Al-Adami told us, in Mecca, Muhammad bin Uthman bin Abi Shaybah told us, Ali bin Hashim told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Laila, on the authority of Al-Hakam, and Issa, on the authority of Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abi Laila, on the authority of Ali, that he said: O Abu Laila, were you not with us in Khaybar? He said: Yes, by God, I was with you. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “sent Abu Bakr to Khaybar, and he marched with the people and was defeated until “He returned.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4338 - True
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4338 - True"
"4339","Maimun bin Ishaq bin Al-Hasan Al-Hashimi told us, in Baghdad, Ahmed bin Abdul-Jabbar Al-Attardi told us, Yunus bin Bukair told us, Al-Musayyab bin Muslim Al-Azdi, Abdullah bin Buraidah narrated to us, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with them both, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was Perhaps his sister took him, and he stayed for a day and two days without going out. When he went down to Khaybar, his sister took him, and he did not go out to the people. And that Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him, took the banner of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, then he got up and fought a fierce fight, then returned. This is a hadith. The chain of narration is authentic, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4339 - True"
"4340","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us about Marwa, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, Nu’aym bin Hakim told us, on the authority of Abi Musa Al-Hanafi, on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him, said: “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, walked to Khaybar, and when he reached it, he sent for Umar, may God Almighty be pleased with him. He sent people with him to their city or palace, and they fought them, and they did not soon defeat Omar and his companions, so they came to make him cowardly. And he makes them cowardly, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, followed the Hadith. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4340 - True"
"4341","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Salman Al-Faqih told us, in Baghdad, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Suleiman told us, Al-Qasim bin Abi Shaybah told us, Yahya told us Ibn Ya`la, Maqil Ibn Ubayd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, may God be pleased with him, “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, pushed the standard on the Day of Khaybar To Omar, may God be pleased with him, and he set off and returned, making his companions cowardly and they making him cowardly. This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4341 - Al-Qasim bin Abi Shaybah is weak"
"4342","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, dictating, Zakaria bin Yahya bin Marwan and Ibrahim bin Ismail Al-Suyuti told us, They said: Fudayl bin Abdul Wahhab narrated to us, Ja’far bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Khalil bin Murrah, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, May God be pleased with them both. He said: On the Day of Khaybar, the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sent a man who was cowardly, so Muhammad bin Maslamah came and said: Oh Messenger of God, I have never seen Mahmoud bin Maslamah killed like today, so the Messenger of God said: “Do not hope to meet the enemy, and ask God for well-being. For you do not know what you will be tested with them, and when you meet them, say: Oh God, you are our Lord and their Lord, and our counsels and their counsels are in your hand. But it is you who kill them. Then they remained seated on the ground, but when they cheated on you, then stand up and be proud.” Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Tomorrow I will send a man who loves God and His Messenger and who loves him, who will not turn his back. God will open his hands.” So the people were honored for her, and Ali, may God be pleased with him. On that day, he turned white, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “Walk.” He said: O Messenger of God, I have never seen a place that spit in his eyes. He held him and gave him the flag, and Ali said: O Messenger of God, why should I fight them? He said: “On the condition that they bear witness that there is no god but God, and that I am the Messenger of God. If they do that, then their blood and their money will be saved from me.” “Except as they deserve, and their reckoning is with God Almighty.” He said: Then he met them, and God granted him victory. “The two sheikhs agreed to narrate the hadith about the banner, and they did not They bring it out in this context.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4342 - They took out the mention of the banner from it"
"4343","Ahmad bin Ja’far al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Abd al-Samad bin Abdul-Warith told us, Ikrimah bin Ammar, Iyas bin Salamah told us, he said: My father told me, saying: “We witnessed with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, Khaybar, when the Messenger of God spat May God’s prayers and peace be upon him in the eyes of Ali, and he was healed, so he gave him the banner. Then Marhab appeared and said:
 [The sea of rage]
 Khaybar has learned that I am welcome... He who wields weapons is a proven hero.
 When wars come, they will rage
 He said: Then Ali, may God be pleased with him, appeared to him and said:
 [The sea of rage]
 I am the one my mother called me Haidara... like a forest clutter with an unpleasant appearance.
 I will recompense you with a Saa’ equivalent to a pound
 He said: He struck Marhab and cut off his head and killed him, and the opening was: “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it in this context.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4343 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"4344","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told me, Ibn Abi Al-Zinad told me, On the authority of his father, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah bin Utbah bin Masoud, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace May God grant him peace and grant him peace upon his sword, Dhul-Faqar, on the day of Badr. This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it. I only mentioned it in this place due to weak information that Dhul-Faqar is from Khaybar.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4344 - True"
"4345","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Abu Ahmad told us, we told him Sufyan, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: “Safiya, may God be pleased with her, was one of the Safis.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4345 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4346","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Yahya bin Abi Bukayr told us, Abu Ja’far Al-Razi told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abi Laila said: I heard Ali, may God be pleased with him, say: “And because I was the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, a fifth of the fifth, I put it in Its context is the life of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Abu Bakr and Omar, may God be pleased with them. This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4346 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4347","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, he said: Thawr told me Bin Yazid, on the authority of Salim, the servant of Abdullah bin Muti’, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: We departed with the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He delivered on the authority of Khaybar to Wadi al-Qura, with him a servant of his who had been given to him by Rifa’ah ibn Zayd al-Hazami. While he was setting up, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, departed. May God bless him and grant him peace. As the sun was setting, a western arrow came to him and killed him. It was an arrow that did not know who shot it. So We said to him: Congratulations to him in Paradise. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “No, by the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, his veil will now burn over him in the fire, its harvest from the spoils of the Muslims.” On the Day of Khaybar, a man from the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came and was terrified when he heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say that, so he said: O Messenger of God, I took two hooks for my sandals, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The like of them will be added to you in Hell.” This is an authentic hadith. The chain of transmission is on the condition of Muslim, and they did not narrate it. “But they agreed on the hadith of Malik, on the authority of Thawr ibn Yazid. With this chain of transmission, we went to Khaybar.” We did not gain any gold or silver. Hadith
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4347 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"4348","Zaid bin Ali bin Yunus Al-Khuza’i told me, in Kufa, Al-Hussein bin Muhammad bin Musab Al-Bajli told me, Ahmad bin Daoud told us, Omar bin Abd told us. Al-Ghafar, narrated by Al-A’mash, on the authority of Adi bin Thabit, on the authority of Al-Bara’ bin Aazib, may God be pleased with them, who said: “When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came Jafar was killed inside of him because of that, so Gabriel came to him and said: God Almighty gave Jafar two wings covered with blood with which he flies with the angels. “This is a hadith that has multiple narrations, on the authority of Al-Baraa, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4348 - All of them are weak on the authority of Al-Bara’"
"4349","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, he said: Abdul Rahman told us Ibn al-Qasim, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: When the death of Ja`far came to him, may God be pleased with him, we recognized him in the face of the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He was sad, and someone entered upon him and said: O Messenger of God, women have been tempted or defeated by us. He said: “Then return to them.” So he silenced them.” So he went, then returned to them and returned them three times. He said: “Go back to them, and if they refuse, put dust in their mouths.” She said. Aisha, may God be pleased with her, and I said to myself to the man: May God keep you away. I know how obedient you are to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And you did not abandon yourself until you realized that you could not put dust into their mouths. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4349 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"4350","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told me, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told me, Muhammad bin Bashar told us, Abd al-Wahhab told us, Khalid al-Hadha told us, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: “He did not wear sandals, nor did he put on shoes, nor rode on mounts after the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Better than Ja’far bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4350 - according to Al-Bukhari’s condition"
"4351","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Shazan Al-Jawhari told us, Zakaria bin Adi told us, Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Safwan bin Amr, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Jubayr bin Nufayr, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with him, who said: When the anxiety of the companions of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, intensified And he greeted whoever was killed on the Day of Death. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The Antichrist will overtake people like you or better than you - three times.” “And God will never disgrace a nation. I am the first of it, and Jesus, son of Mary, is the last of it.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4351 - This is mursal and it is objectionable news"
"4352","Abu Sa`id Ahmad ibn Ya`qub al-Thaqafi told us, Yusuf ibn Ya`qub al-Qadi told us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr told us, Umar ibn Ali told us, on the authority of Ismail ibn Abi Khaled, on the authority of Amer, who said: Ibn Omar, may God be pleased with them both, was alive, and he said: Peace be upon you. O son of Dhul-Janayn, “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.” I have mentioned the virtues of Ja’far bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him. “On his authority, so that I may mention it among the virtues of the Companions, may God be pleased with them all.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4352 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4353","Abu Sa`id Ahmad ibn Ya`qub al-Thaqafi told us, Yusuf ibn Ya`qub al-Qadi told us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr told us, Umar ibn Ali told us, on the authority of Ismail ibn Abi Khaled, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Abdullah Al-Muzani, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Hadrami, on the authority of Saeed bin Amr Al-Ash’athi, on the authority of us. Abther, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Al-Nu’man bin Bashir, may God be pleased with them both, who said: “Abdullah bin Rawahah, may God be pleased with them, fainted.” On the authority of him, his sister Amra started crying: Bye bye brother, by such and such, and so and so kept repeating to him, and he said: When he recovered, I did not say anything except that it was said to me: You. Likewise, “the chain of transmission is authentic, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4353 - True"
"4354","Abu Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Qais Ibn Abi Hazim said: I heard Khalid Ibn Al-Walid saying: “Nine swords fell into my hand on the day of Mu’tah, and all that remained in my hand was a plate.” Yemeni » This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it. « The two sheikhs agreed on the hadith of Humayd bin Hilal, on the authority of Anas bin Malik May God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the Battle of Mu’tah, “Zayd ibn Harithah took the banner and was wounded, then Ja`far took it and was injured, then Abdullah bin Rawahah took it and was injured, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent Khalid bin Al-Walid, may God be pleased with him, until death
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4354 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4355","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, he said: Abdul told me Allah bin Abi Bakr bin Amr bin Hazm, on the authority of Amer bin Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Umm Salamah, may God be pleased with her, that she said To the wife of Salama bin Hisham bin Al-Mughirah: “Why should I not see Salama attending prayer with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and with the Muslims?” She said: By God, he is not able to go out. Whenever he goes out, people shout at him: Oh Farrar, you ran away in the name of God Almighty until he stayed in his house. He did not narrate it, and he was in the Battle of Mu’tah with Khalid bin Al-Walid, may God be pleased with him. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4355 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"4356","Abu Abdullah Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Jahm told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Faraj told us, Al-Waqidi told us, Khalid bin Ilyas told us, on the authority of Al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: “There was a conversation between me and a cousin of mine, and he said: Except for your flight on the Day of Mu’tah, and I did not know “Anything I can tell him.”"
"4357","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Mundhir bin Tha’labah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraidah, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with them both, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent Amr bin Al-Aas to The Battle of Dhat al-Silsil, and among them were Abu Bakr and Omar, may God be pleased with them. When they reached the place of war, Amr ordered them not to light the fire. Then, Omar became angry and was about to attack it, but Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him, forbade him and told him that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had not used it. And peace be upon him, except for his knowledge of the war, so Omar, may God be pleased with him, calmed him down. This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4357 - True"
"4358","Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi told me, Muawiyah ibn Amr told me, Abu Ishaq al-Fazari told me, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Abi Hafs, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Abdullah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: “The conquest took place for thirteen days without Ramadan
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4358 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4359","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, he said: Al-Zuhri told me, On the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah bin Utbah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and his companions departed In the year of conquest, ten thousand Muslims descended upon Dhahran, and Sulaim and Mazina followed, and in all the tribes there were numbers and Islam. He traveled with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, the Muhajireen and the Ansar, but not one of them left him behind, and the news was overwhelming. Quraysh, so no news of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, reaches them, nor do they know what he is doing. Abu Sufyan bin Al-Harith and Abdullah bin Abu Umayyah bin Al-Mughirah met the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, at Thaniyat Al-Aqab between Mecca and Medina, and they sought to enter him. Then Umm Salamah spoke to him and said: O Messenger of God, your cousin, your paternal aunt’s son, and your brother-in-law. He said: “I have no need of them, as for my cousin.” So you violated my honor, and as for my cousin and brother-in-law, he is the one,He told me what he said in Mecca.” When the news got out to them about that, and with Abu Sufyan bin Al-Harith, his son, he said: By God, the Messenger of God will give permission. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, or I will take this son of mine by the hand, and then we will go through the land until we die of thirst or hunger. When that was reported to the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he felt compassion for them, so they entered upon him, and Abu Sufyan reassured him about what he had said about his conversion to Islam, and his apology for what he had gone through, and he said:
 [Long Sea]

 By your age, one day I will carry a banner... for the horses of Al-Lat to defeat the horses of Muhammad
 How dark is the night for the roller coaster of confusion... This is the time for truth. Be guided and be guided.
 So say to Thaqif, “I do not want to fight you.” And say to Thaqif, “This is with me, so promise me.”
 A guide other than myself guided me and directed me...to God whom I have driven away every retaliation.
 I quickly and diligently flee from Muhammad... and claim, even if I do not belong to Muhammad
 They are a group of those who do not speak according to their desires... even if they have an opinion that can be blamed and refuted.
 I want to please them, and I will not be verbally verbal with the people unless I am guided in every seat.
 I was not in the army that won Amir... nor did I tire of the goodness of my tongue or my hand.
 Tribes that came from far away lands... The aftershocks that came from arrows and arrows.
 And the one whom you brought out and insulted... will strive for you with the effort of a person who is not seated.He said: When the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, recited: To God whom I expel every one who expels, the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, struck him in the chest. He said: “You have expelled me every time I have ever been expelled.” Ibn Ishaq said: “The mother of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, died at a young age while she was visiting her maternal uncle.” “From Banu al-Najjar.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it. “And Abu Sufyan bin al-Harith, the brother of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. From breastfeeding, they were breastfed by Halima, and his cousin. Then he treated the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, with ugly treatment, and satirized him more than once until he answered him. Hassan bin Thabit, may God be pleased with him, with his poem in which he says:
 [abundant sea]

 You satirized Muhammad and I responded to him...and with God is the reward for that
 The hadith and the lengthy poem are narrated in the authentic hadith of Muslim, may God Almighty have mercy on him, and it was Hassan bin Thabit, may God be pleased with him. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, asked permission to satire him, but he was not given permission.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4359 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"4360","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Salman Al-Faqih told us, in Baghdad, Abu Dawud Suleiman bin Al-Ash’ath told us, Othman bin Abi Shaybah told me, he told me Ahmad ibn al-Fadl, told us by Asbat ibn Nasr, who said: Al-Suddi claimed, on the authority of Mus’ab ibn Sa’d, on the authority of Sa’d, who said: When it was the day of the conquest of Mecca Abdullah bin Saad bin Abi Sarh hid with Othman bin Affan, may God be pleased with him, and he brought him and made him stand before the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He greeted him, and said: O Messenger of God, pledge allegiance to Abdullah. He raised his head and looked at him three times, then he turned to his companions and said: “Wasn’t he among you? Is a sensible man going to do this when he sees that I have withheld my hand from pledging allegiance to him and kill him?” They said: We do not know, O Messenger of God, what is in your mind. Did you not gesture to us with your eyes? He said: “It is not appropriate for a prophet to have traitorous eyes.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4360 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"4361","Bakr bin Muhammad Al-Sayrifi told us, about Marwa, Ibrahim bin Hilal told us, Ali bin Al-Hassan bin Shaqiq told us, Al-Hussein bin Waqid told us, on the authority of Yazid Al-Nahwi, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them, said: “Abdullah bin Abi Sarh used to write to the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And he joined the infidels, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered him to be killed, so Uthman, may God be pleased with him, sought protection for him, and the Messenger of God granted him protection. “It is authentic according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4361 - According to Al-Bukhari’s condition"
"4362","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, he said: He told me Shurahbil bin Saad said: “It was revealed about Abdullah bin Abi Sarh”: “And who is more unjust than he who invents a lie about God or says, ‘It has been revealed to me,’ and it has not been revealed.” And whoever says, “I will send down the like of what God has sent down” [Al-An’am: 93] When “the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered Mecca, he fled to Uthman ibn Affan, may God be pleased with him, was his foster brother, so he was absent from his presence until the people of Mecca were satisfied, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, brought him And he was safe.” Al-Hakim said: “The narration has been authenticated in both books that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave an order before entering Mecca. By killing Abdullah bin Saad and Abdullah bin Khatal, who looked into the killing of the Commander of the Faithful, Othman bin Affan, may God be pleased with him? And the crimes of Abdullah bin Saad upon him in Egypt until his situation was resolved, and it was not known that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, knew about it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4362 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4363","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, he said: Yahya bin Abbad bin Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr, on the authority of his father Abbad bin Abdullah, on the authority of Asma’ bint Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq, may God be pleased with them, she said: When it was the year of the conquest and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, descended at Tuwa, Abu Quhafa said to his daughter, who was his youngest son: My daughter, show me to Abu Qubays, who was blinded, so I supervised him, and he said: My daughter, what do you see? She said: I see blackness gathered together and I see a man walking in front of that blackness coming, and he said: Those are the horses, my daughter. Then he said: What do you see? She said: I see the blackness has spread, so he said: Then, by God, you have pushed the horse, so hasten with me to my house, so I left quickly until I brought it down to Al-Abatah, and she had a paper collar around her neck, so someone cut it from her neck, when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered the mosque. Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him, went out until he brought his father leading him. When the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saw him, he said: “Will you leave the sheikh alone?” His house until I come to him. He said: He will walk to you, O Messenger of God. He is more worthy than you walking to him. So he made him sit in his hands. Then the Messenger of God wiped May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he bowed his chest and said: “Be safe, you will be safe.” So he accepted Islam, then Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him, stood up and took his sister by the hand and said: I call upon God and Islam to surround my sister. By God, no one brought it with him. Then he said the second time: I call upon God and Islam to ring my sister. No one brought him, and he said: O brother, take care of your collar, for by God, honesty among people is for a few. This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim. And they did not bring it out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4363 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4364","Abu Abdullah Al-Hussein bin Al-Hasan bin Ayyub Al-Tusi told us, Abu Hatim Muhammad bin Idris told us, Sulayman bin Harb told us, Hammad bin Zaid, Ayoub told us, Abu Qalaba told us, on the authority of Amr bin Salamah, then Abu Qalaba said to me: He is alive, won’t you meet him and hear from him? So I met Omar and he told me the hadith. He said: We were in the passage of people, and the riders were talking to us. We would ask them, “What is this matter and what is it about the people,” and they would say: A prophet who claims that God Almighty sent him, and that God revealed to him such-and-such, and the Arabs blamed the conquest for their conversion to Islam, and they say: Look at him. If he appears, then he is a prophet, then believe him. When it was after the conquest, every people hastened to submit their Islam to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Then he came and stayed with such-and-such, then he came from him and we met him, and he said: I came to you from the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He truly said hello, and that “he commands you to do such-and-such, and when the time for prayer comes, let one of you call the call to prayer, and let the one who most of you recites the Qur’an lead you in prayer.” So they looked. They did not find anyone who recited the Qur’an better than me, so they brought me forward. I was seven or six years old. I used to pray, and when I prostrated, my cloak shrank on me. He said: A woman from the neighborhood said: Cover us, your reader. He said: I covered one of the complexes of Yemen for six or seven dirhams, but I was not happy. With something like my joy over that, “Al-Bukhari narrated this hadith, on the authority of Sulaiman bin Harb, in brief, so I cited it in its length.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4364 - Al-Bukhari included some of it"
"4365","Da'laj ibn Ahmad al-Sijzi told me, Ahmad ibn Ali al-Abar told me, Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami told me, Ja`far ibn Sulaiman told me, about Thabit, on the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, entered Mecca on the day of the Conquest, with his chin on his mount, with his head high.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4365 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4366","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Abu Abbas Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Sa’id told us, Ismail bin Abi Al-Harith told us, Ismail bin Abi Al-Harith told us Jafar bin Aoun, Ismail bin Abi Khalid told us, on the authority of Qays, on the authority of Abu Masoud, that a man spoke to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the day of the conquest, Then he was overcome by trembling, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Take it easy, for I am the son of a woman from Quraysh who used to eat porridge.” An authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4366 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4367","Ahmad bin Salman Al-Faqih told us, in Baghdad, Al-Hasan bin Makram told us, Uthman bin Omar told us, Abdullah bin Amir Al-Aslami told us, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn al-Munkadir, on the authority of Jabir, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, mourned the day of Hunayn al-Ansar, and said: “O people Al-Ansar,” and they answered him: “You are our father and our mother, O Messenger of God.” He said: “Turn your faces to God and to His Messenger.” He will admit you to gardens beneath which rivers flow.” So they approached and were filled with longing until they stared at him like a calamity, their shoulders woven, fighting until God defeated the polytheists “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it, and it is witnessed by the hadith of Al-Mubarak bin Fadalah who”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4367 - True"
"4368","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Ishaq told us, Ismail bin Ishaq al-Qadi told us, Sulaiman bin Harb told us, Mubarak bin Fadalah told us, Al-Hasan told us, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, said: On the day of Hunayn, the people of Mecca and the people of Medina met, and the fighting became intense, so they turned back, retreating, so he wailed. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, confronted the Ansar, and he said: “O Muslims, I am the Messenger of God.” They said: To you, by God, we have come, so they bowed down. their heads, then they fought until God granted victory over them. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4368 - True"
"4369","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, he said: Asim told me Ibn Omar Ibn Qatada, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman Ibn Jabir, on the authority of his father Jabir Ibn Abdullah, may God be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him When he finished conquering Mecca, he went to Hunayn and gathered Malik ibn Awf al-Nasri from the Banu Nasr and Jashm and from Saad ibn Bakr and Awzaa. From Banu Hilal, and people from Banu Amr bin Asim bin Awf bin Amir, and the alliances were distributed with them from Thaqif, and Banu Malik, then he walked They took them to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he went with the money, women, and children. When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, heard about them, he sent Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Hadrad al-Aslami, and he said: “Go and enter with the people until you learn for us some of their knowledge.” So he went in and stayed with them for a day. Or two days, then he came and told him the news, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Omar Ibn Al-Khattab: Don’t you hear what Ibn Ubayy says? Haddad? So Omar said: Ibn Abi Hadrad lied, so Ibn Abi Hadrad said: If you lie to me, then perhaps you have lied to someone better than me, so Omar said: O Messenger of God, Don't you hear what Ibn Abi Hadrad says? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O Umar, you were lost, so God Almighty has guided you.” Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was sent to Safwan bin Umayyah asked him about a hundred armors, and what is good for them from their kit, so he said: Are you usurped, Muhammad? He said: “Rather, it is a bare, guaranteed item until we return it to you.” Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, left and walked. “The chain of transmission is authentic, but they did not bring it out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4369 - True"
"4370","Da`laj bin Ahmad al-Sijzi told us, Abd al-Aziz bin Muawiyah told us, Muhammad bin Jahdham told us, Ismail bin Ja`far told us, Abd told me Al-Rahman bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Suleiman bin Musa Al-Ashdak, on the authority of Makhoul, on the authority of Abu Salam Al-Bahili, may God be pleased with him, the companion of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace Peace and blessings of God be upon him, on the authority of Ubadah ibn al-Samit, may God be pleased with him, who said: On the day of Hunayn, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took a camel’s camel’s shoulder. Then he said: “O people, nothing is permissible for me of what God has bestowed upon you in the amount of these except the fifth, and the fifth will be returned to you, so return the thread.” And the sewing, and beware of deceit, for it will be a disgrace to its people on the Day of Resurrection, and you must wage jihad in the path of God, for it is one of the gates of Paradise, God removes worry and grief with it.” He said: And the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, hated arrogance and said: “That the strong of the believers might be repelled.” On their weak"
"4371","Abu Amr Othman bin Ahmed bin Abdullah Al-Zahid told us, in Baghdad, Abdul Rahman bin Muhammad bin Mansour told us, Muadh bin Hisham, my father told me, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Salim ibn Abi al-Ja’d, on the authority of Ma’dan ibn Abi Talha, on the authority of Abu Najih al-Salami, may God be pleased with him. He said: We besieged the Taif Palace with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “Whoever reaches the level with an arrow will get a degree.” In Paradise” and on that day sixteen arrows reached “and I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “Whoever shoots an arrow in the way of God is liberated justice, and whoever turns gray hair in Islam will have light on the Day of Resurrection, and any Muslim man who frees another Muslim man, God will make all One of His bones is the equivalent of every bone for another from the Fire, and whenever a Muslim woman frees a Muslim woman, God will make every “A bone from its bones is the fulfillment of every bone from the bones of one who freed it from the Fire.” Sahih and high, but they did not bring it out.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4371 - True"
"4372","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Muslim bin Ibrahim told us, Dawud bin Abdul Rahman told us, he said: I heard Amr ibn Dinar narrated, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, performed the Umrah for four lifetimes: The Umrah of Al-Hudaybiyyah, the Umrah of Al-Qadha from Qabil, the third from Al-Jiranah, and the fourth which is accompanied by his proof: “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. And they did not bring it out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4372 - True"
"4373","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, he said: Yazid told me Ibn Sufyan, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Ka’b Al-Qurazi, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Masoud, may God be pleased with him, who said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, walked To Tabuk, a man would still fall behind, and they would say: O Messenger of God, so-and-so has lagged behind, and he would say: “Leave him, if there is good in him, God will overtake him.” And if it is other than that, God has spared you from it.” Until it was said: O Messenger of God, Abu Dharr lagged behind, and his camel slowed him down, so the Messenger of God said God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Leave him. If there is good in him, God will attach him to you, and if there is other than that, God will relieve you of him.” So Abu Dharr blamed May God be pleased with him, he was on his camel, but he slowed down on it. When he slowed down on it, he took his belongings and put them on his back, and he went out following the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. May God bless him and grant him peace. He was walking, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, descended in some of his houses, and a Muslim observer looked and said: O Messenger of God, this is A man was walking on the road, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Be Abu Dharr.” When the people looked at him, they said: O Messenger of God, he is by God. Abu Dharr, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “May God have mercy on Abu Dharr. He walks alone, dies alone, and is resurrected alone.” So he struck. After his death, Abu Dharr walked to Al-Rabdha, and when death approached him, he instructed his wife and his servant, “If I die, wash me and shroud me.” Then they carried me and placed me on the side of the road. The first group of people to pass by you said: This is Abu Dharr. When he died, they did likewise to him, and a group of people appeared. They did not know about him until their knees were almost stepping on his bed. Then they saw Ibn Masoud among a group of the people of Kufa. They said: What is this? It was said: The funeral of Abu Dharr. Then Ibn Masoud, may God be pleased with him, started crying and said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, spoke the truth: “May God have mercy on Abu A progeny who walks alone, dies alone, and is resurrected alone.” So Fulayh descended with himself until he was mad. When they came to Medina, he mentioned Othman had the saying of Abdullah and what was left of it: “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4373 - It has a transmission"
"4374","Ahmed bin Kamil Al-Qadi told us, Ahmed bin Muhammad bin Issa Al-Barti told us, Ishaq bin Bishr Al-Kahili told us, Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Salem Bin Abi Hafsa, on the authority of Jumay bin Umair Al-Laythi, who said: I came to Abdullah bin Umar, may God be pleased with them both, and I asked him about Ali, may God be pleased with them. On his authority, he rebuked me, then said: Shall I not tell you on the authority of Ali? This is the house of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the mosque, and this is the house of Ali, may God be pleased with him. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent Abu Bakr and Omar, may God be pleased with them, went innocently to the people of Mecca, and they set off. They saw a rider, and they said: Who is this? He said: I am Ali, Abu Bakr. Give me the letter that you have. He said: What is mine? He said: By God, I have only known good things. So Ali took the letter and took it, and Abu Bakr and Omar, may God be pleased with them, returned to Medina. They said: What do we have, O Messenger of God? He said: “There is nothing but good for you, but I was told: No one will report on your behalf except you or a man from among you.” This is an abnormal hadith and the blame for it is on everyone. Bin Umair and after him, after Ishaq bin Bishr.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4374 - abnormal"
"4375","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Al-Hussein bin Ali bin Shabib Al-Amri told me, Ibrahim bin Ziyad Sablan told us, Abbad told us Ibn Al-Awwam, on the authority of Sufyan Ibn Hussein, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Miqsam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him He sent Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him, and ordered him to pronounce these words. So Ali followed him, and Abu Bakr passed us some way, when He heard the moaning of the she-camel of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so Abu Bakr came out in fright, and thought that he was the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Ali, so the letter of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was given to him, instructing him about the season, and he ordered Ali to pronounce these words, so Ali stood up. During the days of the Tashreeq, he called out: “Indeed, God is free from the polytheists, and His Messenger is free of them. So travel around the land for four months. No polytheist will perform Hajj after the year, nor They will circumambulate the House naked, and no one will enter Paradise except a believer.” So Ali used to call out about it, and when he became angry, Abu Hurairah stood up and called out, “Sahih The chain of transmission, and they did not narrate it, and the narration was authentic, on the authority of Ali, explaining this call.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4375 - True"
"4376","Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Ishaq and Ali ibn Hamshadh told us, they said: Bishr ibn Musa told me, Al-Humaydi told us, Sufyan told me, Abu told me Ishaq Al-Hamdani, on the authority of Zayd bin Yatha’, who said: We asked Ali, may God be pleased with him, for what purpose you were sent for the Hajj. He said: “I was sent with four: No. Only a believing soul will enter Paradise, and no naked person will circumambulate the House, and no believer and an unbeliever will gather in the Sacred Mosque after their year, this, Whoever has a covenant with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, then his covenant lasts for its duration, and whoever does not have a covenant, his period is four months. “It is authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4376 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4377","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, he said: Saad told me Ibn Tariq, on the authority of Salamah ibn Nu`aym ibn Masoud, on the authority of his father, who said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying, “When a messenger came to him, Muslim... He is a liar by his book, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, says to them: “And you say the same as what he says?” They said: Yes, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “By God, if messengers were not killed, I would have struck your necks.” This is an authentic hadith according to The condition of a Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4377 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"4378","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Muhammad bin Abdul-Wahhab told us, Ja’far bin Aoun told us, Abd al-Rahman bin Abdullah Al-Masoudi, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abdulrahman bin Abdullah Al-Masoudi, on the authority of his father, who said: A man came to Abdullah bin Masoud, may God be pleased with him, said: O Abu Abdul Rahman, there are people here who are reciting from Musaylamah’s recitation, so Abdullah said: “A book other than the Book of God, or a Messenger other than the Messenger of God after the spread of Islam?” He sent him back, then he came to him later and said: O Abdullah, by the One besides Whom there is no god, they are at home reciting the Qur’an as Musaylimah recites, and he is with them. A Qur’an containing easy reading, and that was in the time of Uthman, may God be pleased with him, so Abdullah said to Qardha, who was a horse owner: “Go until It surrounds the house and takes whoever is in it.” So he did so, and eighty men came to him, and Abdullah said to them: “Woe to a book other than the book of God Almighty, or A messenger other than the Messenger of God? They said: We repent to God, for we have been wronged. So Abdullah left them and did not fight them, and led them to the Levant, except for their leader, Ibn al-Nawahah. He refused to repent, so Abdullah said to Qarzah: “Go and behead him, and lay his head on his mother’s lap, for I see that she knew what he did.” So he did.” Then Abdullah started narrating a hadith and said: This man and Ibn Uthāl came as two messengers from Musaylimah to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “Do you bear witness that I am the Messenger of God?” He said to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: You bear witness that Musaylimah is the Messenger of God, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If it were not that you are the Messenger of “I would have killed you.” The Sunnah was established at that time that a Messenger should not be killed. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. They did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4378 - True"
"4379","Abu Saeed Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told us, Muhammad bin Hayyan Al-Ansari told us, Shayban bin Farukh told us, Mubarak bin Fadalah told us, Al-Hasan told us, On the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to Musaylimah, and Musaylimah said to him: Do you bear witness that I am the Messenger of God? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I believe in God and His messengers.” Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “This is another man.” “For the destruction of his people.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4379 - True"
"4380","Abu Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, he said: Muhammad told me Ibn Al-Walid Ibn Nuwaifa’, on the authority of Kurayb, the client of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: Banu Sa’d Ibn Bakr was sent Dimam ibn Tha'labah went to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he came to us and leaned his camel at the door of the mosque, and it stopped, then he entered upon the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him while he was in the mosque, sitting with his companions, and he said: Which of you is Ibn Abdul-Muttalib? The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “ I am Ibn Abdul Muttalib. He said: Muhammad? He said: “Yes.” He said: O Muhammad, I am asking you and will be harsh on you in the matter, so do not find it in yourself to be against me, for I do not find it in myself. He said: “Ask about whatever seems to you.” He said: “I adjure you by God, your God and the God before you, and the God of the one who will exist after you. Has God sent you to us as a messenger?” He said: “By God, yes.” He said: I adjure you by God, your God, and the God before you, and the God of those who will exist after you. God has commanded you to That we worship Him and do not associate anything with Him, and that we cast off these idols and enemies that our fathers used to worship? Then he, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said, “O God,” “Yes,” and then he began to mention the duties of Islam, an obligation of prayer, an obligation.Zakat, fasting, Hajj, and the obligatory duties of Islam, all of which he recites at every obligatory duty, just as he recited them in the ones before them, until When he finished, he said: I bear witness that there is no god but God, and that you are His servant and His Messenger, and I will perform these obligations and avoid what You forbade me from him, neither more nor less. Then he left and returned to his camel, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said when he left: “If he speaks the truth.” He will enter Paradise with two sticks of sticks.” And there was Dimam, a man with hairy skin and two ringlets. Then he brought his camel, and he let go of its reins until he came to his people. So they gathered around him, and the first thing he spoke was when he was cursing Al-Lat and Al-Uzza, and they said: Oh Dammam, beware of leprosy, leprosy, and madness. He said: Woe to you! Indeed, by God, they will neither harm nor benefit. Indeed, God has sent a messenger and sent down to him a book by which He saved you from what you were. In it, and I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger, and that I have come to you from Him with what He commanded you and prohibited you. On his behalf, by God, there was not a man or a woman in his presence that evening except a Muslim.Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them, said: We have never heard of a people coming who was better than Dimmam bin Tha’labah, may God be pleased with him. “And he agreed The two sheikhs cited the narration of the dhammam of Medina, and neither of them cited the hadith in its entirety, and this is true.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4380 - True"
"4381","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Shabib Al-Maamari told me, Abu Musa Ishaq bin Musa told us Al-Ansari, Abdullah bin Nafi’ narrated to us, Nafi’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Umar, may God be pleased with them both, “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, performed Hajj in the year From his beginning to Medina, he performed the Hajj alone.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4381 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4382","Abu Bakr bin Abi Darim Al-Hafiz told me, Abu Al-Abbas Ahmad bin Abdullah bin Shuja’ Al-Baghdadi told us, Qasim bin Muhammad bin Abbad bin Abbad Al-Muhallabi, Abdullah bin Dawud Al-Khuraibi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, who said: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, performed Hajj before he migrated for Hajj. He performed Hajj after his farewell migration, and all he brought with him was one hundred camels, including a camel that had a lump of silver in its nose, which the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, slaughtered. He made sixty-three greetings with his hand, and he slaughtered Ali, may God be pleased with him, forever. It was said to the revolutionary, “Who mentioned him?” He said: Ja`far bin Muhammad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Jabir, and Ibn Abi Laila, on the authority of Miqsam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both. Al-Hakim said: “As for the narrated hadiths that were explained in the Farewell Pilgrimage, the two sheikhs agreed to narrate them with authentic chains of narration. Their condition, and the most correct and complete of them, is the hadith of Ja`far bin Muhammad al-Sadiq, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Jabir, may God be pleased with him, who was the only one to narrate it in Muslim. Ibn al-Hajjaj, and with the will and help of God Almighty we have reached the beginning of the illness of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4382 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4383","Abu Ahmad Bakr bin Muhammad bin Hamdan Al-Sayrifi told us, citing the origin of his book, Abu Ismail Muhammad bin Ismail told us Al-Tirmidhi, Omar bin Abdul-Wahhab Al-Riyahi Abu Hafs told us, Ibrahim bin Saad bin Ibrahim Al-Zuhri told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Umar ibn Hafs told me, on the authority of Ubayd ibn Hunayn, the client of Al-Hakam ibn Abi Al-Aas, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Amr ibn Al-Aas, may God be pleased with him. May God bless them both, on the authority of Abu Muwayhibah, the servant of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, knocked on me one night. He said: “O Abu Muwayhibah, go and ask forgiveness, for I have been commanded to ask forgiveness for the people of this Al-Baqi’.” So I set off with him, and when he reached Al-Baqi’, He said: “Peace be upon you, O people of Al-Baqi’. The temptations you have arrived in will be easy for you, if only you knew what God has saved you from. The temptations have come in pieces. The dark night follows its beginning with its last.” Then he said: “O Abu Muwayhibah, God has chosen for me to give me the treasures of the earth and immortality.” Therein, then Paradise and the meeting with my Lord Almighty.” So I said: May my father and mother be sacrificed for you, take the keys to the treasures of this earth and abide therein forever. Paradise, he said: “No, Abu Muwayhiba, I have chosen to meet my Lord, the Almighty and Majestic.” Then he asked forgiveness for the people of Al-Baqi’, then he left. When the morning became It began with his complaint in which he, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was arrested: “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, except that he was astonished by this chain of narration.”"
"4384","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us from the origin of his book, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, He said: Abdullah bin Rabi’ah told me, on the authority of Ubaid bin Abdul-Hakam, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, on the authority of Abu Muwayhibah Radi God, on their authority, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and something similar.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4383 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"4385","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz narrated to us, Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Al-Nadr bin Maslamah bin Al-Jaroud narrated to me, Al-Zubair bin Bakkar, Yahya bin Al-Miqdam told me, on the authority of his uncle, Musa bin Yaqoub, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Ishaq, on the authority of al-Zuhri, that Urwah bin Al-Zubayr, Al-Qasim bin Muhammad bin Abi Bakr, Abu Bakr bin Abdul Rahman bin Al-Harith bin Hisham, and Ubaid Allah bin Abdullah bin Utba, all of them tell him, on the authority of Aisha, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, began his illness in which he died.” With him in the house of Maimuna, may God be pleased with her, he went out with his head tied, and Ali entered between two men whose feet crossed the ground, on his right was Abbas. And on his left is a man.” Ubayd Allah said: Ibn Abbas told me, “The one on his left is Ali.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it. I mentioned above the disagreement of the Companions, may God be pleased with them, regarding the age of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the day he died.”"
"4386","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Ubayy and Shuaib bin Al-Layth bin Saad told us, on the authority of Al-Layth, on the authority of Yazid ibn al-Had, on the authority of Musa ibn Sarjis, on the authority of al-Qasim, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, dies and he has a cup of water in it. He puts his hand into the cup, then wipes his face with water, and then says: “O God, help me for my drunkenness.” “Death” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4386 - True"
"4387","Ahmad bin Kamil Al-Qadi told us, Al-Hussein bin Ali bin Abdul-Samad Al-Bazzaz Al-Farisi told us, Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, Al-Mu’tamir told us Bin Sulaiman, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, the last thing he spoke was: “The majesty of my Lord is exalted. I have conveyed the message.” Then, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he ruled, “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, except that this Persian is mistaken about it according to Muhammad ibn Abd.” the highest"
"4388","Abu Al-Hasan Ahmad bin Muhammad Al-Anazi narrated to us, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi narrated to us, Al-Nufaili narrated to us, Zuhair narrated to us, and others narrated to us, on the authority of Suleiman Al-Taymi, On the authority of Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, he said: The last commandment of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace when death approached him, was “to pray, to pray,” twice. “And as long as your right hands possess it,” and he continued to gargle it in his chest while his tongue was overflowing with it, “they have agreed to narrate this hadith, and to narrate The hadith of Aisha, the last word spoken by the “Supreme Companion”"
"4389","Al-Hussein bin Al-Hasan bin Ayyub told us, Abu Hatim Al-Razi told us, Abu Zafar told us, Ja’far bin Suleiman told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him. On his authority, he said: “On the day on which the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, died, everything was darker than Medina.” This is an authentic hadith on the condition that Muslim, and they did not produce it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4389 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"4390","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl, Al-Adl, told us, Hisham bin Ali told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Khuza’i, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Thabit, On the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him, he said: “I witnessed the day on which the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, died, and I have not seen a day uglier than it.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4390 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"4391","Abu Ja`far Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Baghdadi told us, Abdullah ibn Abdul Rahman ibn al-Murtada al-San’ani told us, Abu Al-Walid Al-Makhzoumi, Anas bin Iyad told us, on the authority of Jafar bin Muhammad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with them both, who said: “When The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed away. The angels consoled them. They hear the senses but do not see the person. They said: Peace be upon you, People of the House. By God’s mercy and blessings, in God is a solace from every calamity, and a successor from every calamity, so trust in God, and hope in Him, for only the deprived Whoever is deprived of reward, may the peace, mercy, and blessings of God be upon you. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4391 - True"
"4392","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Balawayh told us, Muhammad bin Bishr bin Matar told us, Kamil bin Talha told us, Abbad bin Abdul Samad told us, On the authority of Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, he said: “When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was arrested, his companions stared at him and cried around him. They gathered together, and a man with a red beard, handsome and handsome, entered and touched their necks and cried. Then he turned to the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And he greeted, and said: In God there is a solace from every calamity, a compensation for every loss, and a successor from every perishing, so to God, then repent, and to Him, hope. And we look at you in the affliction, so take heed, for the afflicted one is he who was not repressed. “And he departed, and some of them said to one another: Do you know the man? Abu Bakr and Ali said: Yes, this is the brother of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, Al-Khidr, peace be upon him. “This is evidence of what was mentioned above, even if it is Abbad ibn Abd al-Samad is not a condition of this book.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4392 - This is evidence of what came before"
"4393","Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Ashqar told me, Yusuf ibn Musa al-Marwazi told me, Ahmad ibn Salih told us, Anbasa told us, Yunus, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, who said: Urwa said: Aisha, may God be pleased with her, used to say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say during his illness On which he died: “O Aisha, I feel pain from the food I ate in Khaybar. This is the time for my aorta to stop from that poison.” This hadith It is authentic according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and Al-Bukhari included it and said: And Yunus said:
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4393 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4394","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abdullah bin Murrah, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah, may God be pleased with him, who said: “Because I swear nine times that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was killed, I love I had to swear once that he would not be killed, and that is because God Almighty took him as a prophet and took him as a martyr.” This is an authentic hadith on the authority of The condition of the two sheikhs and they did not include it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4394 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4395","Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi narrated to us more than once, Abd al-Samad ibn al-Fadl al-Balkhi narrated to us, Makki ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Dawud ibn Yazid Al-Awdi said: I heard Al-Sha’bi saying: “By God, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was poisoned, Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq was poisoned, and Omar bin Al-Khattab was patient, Othman bin Affan was killed patiently, Ali bin Abi Talib was killed patiently, Al-Hasan bin Ali was poisoned, and Al-Hussein bin Ali was killed Patience, may God be pleased with them, for what we can hope for after them.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4395 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4396","Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Balawayh told me, Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal told me, my father told me, Abd al-Razzaq told me, he informed me Muammar, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, “Fatima, the daughter of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, cried to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: ‘Oh “His father, what has brought him closer from his Lord? O my father, to Gabriel, call him. O my father, the Garden of Firdaus is his abode.” This is an authentic hadith on the condition that The two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4396 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4397","Abd al-Rahman bin Hamdan al-Jallab told us, in Hamdan, Ibrahim bin Nasr al-Razi and Ibrahim bin Dezil told us, they said: Sulayman bin Harb, Hammad bin Zayd narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him, who said: “I washed the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace peace be upon him, so I started to look at what was of the dead, but I did not see anything, and he was good, both alive and dead, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him.” This is an authentic hadith on the authority of The conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not include it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4397 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4398","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, he said: Yahya told me Ibn Abbad Ibn Abdullah Ibn Al-Zubayr, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: “We wanted to wash the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him.” Then the people disagreed about it, and some of them said: We strip the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, as we strip our dead, or we wash him with his clothes on. So God imposed upon them the Sunnah until there was not a man among them but sleeping with his chin on his chest. Then someone from the direction of the house said: Do you not know that the Messenger of Is God, may God bless him and grant him peace, washed and has his clothes on? So they washed him with his shirt on, pouring water over him and massaging it from above. Aisha, may God be pleased with her, said: “By God, if “I have received from my affairs what I have taken care of. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not wash except his wives.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and it was not “He brings him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4398 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4399","Hamza bin Muhammad bin Al-Abbas Al-Aqbi told us, in Baghdad, Abdullah bin Ruh Al-Madaini told us, Salam bin Sulayman Al-Madaini told us, Salam bin Sulayman Al-Madaini told us, Salam bin Sulayman Al-Madaini told us. Ibn Sulaym al-Taweel, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of al-Hasan al-Urni, on the authority of al-Ash’ath ibn Taliq, on the authority of Murrah ibn Sharahil, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, may God be pleased with him, said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, became heavy, we said: Who will pray for you, O Messenger of God? He cried. We cried and he said: “Wait, may God forgive you and reward you well on behalf of your Prophet. If you wash me, embalm me, and shroud me, then place me on the edge of My grave, then leave me for an hour, for the first to pray over me are my friends and companions, Gabriel and Michael, then Israfil, then the Angel of Death with armies of angels, then let the men of my household begin to pray over me, then their women, then they enter in groups, groups and individually, and no You hurt me with weeping, or crying, or with a cry, and whoever of my companions is absent, extend my greetings to him, for I bear witness to you that I have greeted Whoever enters Islam, and whoever follows me in this religion from today until the Day of Resurrection.” Abd al-Malik ibn Abd al-Rahman, who is in This chain of narration is unknown, we do not know it to be fair or reliable, and the rest are all trustworthy.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4399 - Abd al-Malik, unknown"
"4400","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih and Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, saying: Bishr bin Musa told us, Al-Humaydi told us, Sufyan told us, he said: I heard Yahya bin Saeed narrates, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyib, who said: Aisha, may God be pleased with her, said: “I saw as if three moons had fallen in My room, so I asked Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him, and he said: O Aisha, if you believe your visions, the three best people on earth will be buried in your house. When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was arrested and buried, Abu Bakr said to me: O Aisha, this is the best of your moons, and he is one of them. “This is a hadith. It is authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it. We have written it from the hadith of Anas bin Malik with a chain of transmission.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4400 - according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4401","Ali bin Hamshadh told us, Junaid bin Hakim Al-Daqqaq told us, Musa bin Abdullah Al-Sulami told us, Omar bin Hammad bin Saeed Al-Abh told us, on the authority of Ibn Abu Orouba, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was amazed by the vision. He said: “Has any of you seen “Today’s vision.” Aisha, may God be pleased with her, said: I saw as if three moons had fallen into my room, so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to her: He said: “If your visions come true, three of the best or best people on earth will be buried in your house.” When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, died and was buried in Her house. Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him, said to her: This is one of your moons and he is the best of her. Then Abu Bakr and Omar died and were buried in her house."
"4402","Ahmad ibn Ja`far al-Quta’i informed us, Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal informed us, my father informed me, Hammad ibn Usama informed us, Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: “I was entering my house in which the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was in it, and I was laying My dress and I said: It is my husband and my father. When Omar was buried with them, by God, I did not enter unless my clothes were tied around me, ashamed of Omar’s contentment. May God bless him and grant him peace, “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”"
